==================================================

- Output only valid JSON.
- Do not include markdown code fences.
- Do not mention "explicit", "inferred", or "uncertainty" as labels.
- Integrate reasoning naturally into the specification.
- Be concise but information-dense.
- Target 300–350 words for `final_task_requirement`.
- Do not exceed 350 words.
- Maintain a consistent expert-level voice.
- Avoid generic boilerplate.
- Avoid overfitting to superficial dataset fields.
- Do not invent hidden fields, unavailable tools, backend capabilities, or automation requirements.
- Do not introduce formulas, thresholds, weighted scoring, or rigid filtering unless the user asks for them.
- Do not introduce a new final output artifact merely because it would improve interpretability.
- Do not make traceability, conflict reporting, scoring, annotation, UI design, or summarization central unless the user’s instruction makes it central.

